{"term":"elite","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:be5385f3f0e5e4fea8","definition":"Of high birth or social position; aristocratic or patrician.","example":"","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["antielite","anti-elite","counterelite","elitarian","elite ball knowledge","elite capture","elitedom","eliteness","elite overproduction","eliticide","elitocracy","nonelite","subelite","superelite","unelite"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elite#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d274b238961e9b73ea","definition":"Representing the choicest or most select of a group.","example":"Not since Coventry in 1992 has a Premier League side kicked off a campaign with an all-English XI but things have reached the point where, of the 61 signings who have cost the elite division's 20 clubs a transfer fee this summer, only 12 have involved Englishmen.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["antielite","anti-elite","counterelite","elitarian","elite ball knowledge","elite capture","elitedom","eliteness","elite overproduction","eliticide","elitocracy","nonelite","subelite","superelite","unelite"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elite#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2540d2c5e7cb54f865","definition":"A special group or social class of people who have a superior social or economic status and attendant power, advantages, or privileges in society; a member of such a group.","example":"constituting an elite","pos":"noun","synonyms":["crème de la crème"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["antielite","anti-elite","counterelite","elitarian","elite ball knowledge","elite capture","elitedom","eliteness","elite overproductio